# Plan reference data integrity

This data governs what a licensed agent says to a client on a recorded
call. A wrong benefit value is a regulatory violation, not a bug.
Accuracy and traceability outrank completeness, speed and helpfulness.

## Generated output, never hand-edited

data/plans/*.json (154 files) and data/plan-index.json are built by
scripts/build-plan-profiles.js from the ledger. To change a profile,
change the converter and rebuild with npm run build:profiles.

The converter maps onto 113 keys. Source of truth: `scripts/lib/base-schema.json` (array length 113). Do not add, rename or
remove a key unless told to in the current request.

## Schema invariants

- Every value is a fact leaf: {v, src, pg, sec, url, cur, app, gov, auth,
  conf, vs}. Never a bare string.
- An absent key means never considered. {v: null, vs:
  "NOT_FOUND_IN_SOURCE"} means searched and not found. These are
  different and must never be collapsed into one another.
- NOT_FOUND_IN_SOURCE NEVER MEANS NOT COVERED. It also never means
  covered.
- A dash or N/A in a source benefit grid is NOT_FOUND_IN_SOURCE, not a
  denial.
- Conflicts are recorded, never silently resolved.
- profile_confidence is the weakest fact in the profile, not an average.
- Training material (auth rank 6) can never establish coverage,
  exclusions, waiting periods or pre-existing provisions. It may
  corroborate only.

## Retrieval

Fuzzy matching is permitted on plan names ONLY. Never on benefit text.
The portfolio is roughly 95 percent lexically identical across variants,
so semantic search over benefit text returns confident wrong numbers.

Resolve an exact plan_id first, then read only that plan's data.

Never carry a value from one variant to another however identical the
pages look. Never compare across tiers. The benefit ladder is not
monotonic: a dearer tier is not a superset of a cheaper one.

If the plan or tier is ambiguous, ask and show the options. Never guess.

## Any UI consuming this data

A blank field is a compliance failure, not a cosmetic one. A newer agent
who sees a blank field will fill it in from memory. Every unknown must
render an explicit not-confirmed state.

Compliance and disclosure language must come verbatim from the attached
compliance records. Never compose, paraphrase or improve it.
